cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Semantic Gravity Field Is a Token Prior and a Cosine: Six Falsification Tests for Field-Inspired Attention"
message: "Cite this preprint if you use the artifact."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Junbin
    alias: PD-Dount
    website: "https://github.com/PD-Dount"
repository-code: "https://github.com/PD-Dount/semantic-gravity-field"
url: "https://github.com/PD-Dount/semantic-gravity-field"
abstract: "Physically inspired attention variants that give tokens a mass, a capture radius and a distance-decaying potential promise content-adaptive sparsity. This artifact implements one complete semantic gravity field as a single parameterised attention layer and falsifies its deployment path in six independent tests: an exact algebraic reduction to a softmax attention with a warped cosine logit, equal-parameter ablation with no accuracy difference, gradient-sign voting against the mechanism, a cost ratio that grows with context while effective participation stays flat, bistable dynamics with no multi-cluster state, bit-identical equivalence to LRFU for memory eviction, and an attention-logit fit indistinguishable from parameter-matched controls."
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-10"
keywords:
  - attention
  - negative results
  - reproducibility
  - semantic gravity
  - sparse attention
  - pre-registration
